{"1439":["<div class=\"rb dk nb\" style=\"background:#6a3d8f\"><h4 style=\"color:#fff;background:#6a3d8f;padding:0 .3em;border-radius:4px;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700;background:#6a3d8f;padding:.25em .5em;border-radius:5px\">Unit conversions</h4></div><p style=\"color:#5b6874\">Many wrong options come from a missed ×1000 or ×√3. Convert first, then use the formula.</p><p style=\"color:#6a3d8f;font-size:1.17em;font-weight:700\">Power &amp; energy</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 HP (British) 746 W</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 HP (metric, PS)</td><td>735.5 W</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 kW 1.341 HP</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 kWh</td><td>3.6 MJ = 860 kcal</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 kcal 4.186 kJ = 1.163 Wh</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 unit (electricity)</td><td>1 kWh</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 BTU 1055 J</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 J</td><td>1 W·s = 0.239 cal</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#6a3d8f;font-weight:700\">Electrical prefixes</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 MVA 1000 kVA = 10⁶ VA</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 kA</td><td>1000 A</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 µF 10⁻⁶ F</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 nF</td><td>10⁻⁹ F = 1000 pF</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 mH 10⁻³ H</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 MΩ</td><td>10⁶ Ω</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">I (A) from MVA, kV I = MVA×1000 / (√3 kV)</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">I from kVA at 415 V</td><td>≈ 1.39 × kVA</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#6a3d8f;font-weight:700\">Speed &amp; angle</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 rpm 0.1047 rad/s (×0.1047)</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 rad/s</td><td>9.549 rpm</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 rad 57.296°</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1°</td><td>0.01745 rad</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">π/6, π/4, π/3 30°, 45°, 60°</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 rev</td><td>2π rad = 360°</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 km/h 0.2778 m/s</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 m/s</td><td>3.6 km/h</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#6a3d8f;font-weight:700\">Temperature, length, area</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">K °C + 273</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">°F</td><td>1.8 °C + 32</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 inch 2.54 cm</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 mile</td><td>1.609 km</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 mm² 10⁻⁶ m²</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 cm²</td><td>10⁻⁴ m²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 lux 1 lm/m²</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 foot-candle</td><td>10.76 lux</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#6a3d8f;font-weight:700\">Magnetic &amp; misc</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 Wb/m² 1 T = 10⁴ gauss</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 Wb</td><td>10⁸ maxwell</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 AT/m H unit</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 atm</td><td>101.3 kPa</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 bar 10⁵ Pa</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 kg-wt</td><td>9.81 N</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 litre 10⁻³ m³</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 tonne</td><td>1000 kg</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#6a3d8f;font-weight:700\">Also seen in past questions</td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 kVAr 1000 VAr (reactive)</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 MWh</td><td>1000 kWh = 3.6 GJ</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 GWh 10⁶ kWh</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 Ah</td><td>3600 C</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">760 mm Hg 1 atm = 101.3 kPa</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 hectare</td><td>10⁴ m² = 2.47 acre</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">Specific heat J/(kg·K) · water 4186</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">Calorific value</td><td>kJ/kg (coal ≈ 25 MJ/kg) · gas kJ/m³</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">Moment of inertia kg·m² (J = Σmr²)</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 Mbps</td><td>10⁶ bit/s · 1 kbps = 10³ bit/s</td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 octave · 1 decade f × 2 · f × 10</td><td style=\"font-weight:700\">1 eV · 1 Å</td><td>1.602×10⁻¹⁹ J · 10⁻¹⁰ m</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#6a3d8f;font-weight:700\">Line current, 3-phase (computed)</td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\" style=\"--hc:#6a3d8f\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#6a3d8f\">Rating (415 V)</th><th style=\"background:#6a3d8f\">Current</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>25 kVA</td><td>34.8 A</td></tr><tr><td>63 kVA</td><td>87.6 A</td></tr><tr><td>100 kVA</td><td>139.1 A</td></tr><tr><td>250 kVA</td><td>347.8 A</td></tr><tr><td>500 kVA</td><td>695.6 A</td></tr><tr><td>5 MVA @ 11 kV</td><td>262.4 A</td></tr><tr><td>10 MVA @ 11 kV</td><td>524.9 A</td></tr><tr><td>10 MVA @ 33 kV</td><td>175.0 A</td></tr><tr><td>50 MVA @ 110 kV</td><td>262.4 A</td></tr><tr><td>100 MVA @ 230 kV</td><td>251.0 A</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",[]],"1445":["<h4 style=\"color:#1f4e79;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">Units &amp; conversions</h4><p style=\"color:#555555\">Change any unit in one step: W ↔ kW, Wb, C, F, rad/s ↔ rpm, ° ↔ rad, K, N·m, A/m², dB, SI prefixes.</p><p style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#2f6fd0\">●</span> 1. Power &amp; energy — watt, kW, kWh, HP</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#e8f1fd;color:#2f6fd0\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#e8f1fd;color:#2f6fd0\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#e8f1fd;color:#2f6fd0\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">1 kW</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1000 W</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">2500 W = 2.5 kW · 0.75 kW = 750 W</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">1 MW</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1000 kW = 10⁶ W</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 GW = 1000 MW</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">1 W</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 J/s (joule per second)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">power = energy ÷ time</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">1 kWh = 1 unit</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">3.6 MJ = 3.6 × 10⁶ J</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">100 W lamp for 10 h = 1 kWh</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">1 kWh</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">860 kcal</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 cal = 4.186 J</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">1 HP (metric)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">735.5 W</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 HP (British) = 746 W</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">kW</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">kVA × power factor</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">kVAR = kVA × sin φ</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">1 eV</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1.602 × 10⁻¹⁹ J</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">electron-volt (energy of one electron through 1 V)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#2e8b57\">●</span> 2. Length, area &amp; volume — metre</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#e8f6ea;color:#2e8b57\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#e8f6ea;color:#2e8b57\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#e8f6ea;color:#2e8b57\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 km</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1000 m</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 m = 100 cm = 1000 mm</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 μm · 1 nm · 1 Å</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10⁻⁶ m · 10⁻⁹ m · 10⁻¹⁰ m</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">micron, nanometre, ångström</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 inch · 1 foot</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">2.54 cm · 0.3048 m</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 mile = 1.609 km</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 m²</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10⁶ mm² = 10⁴ cm²</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">2.5 mm² = 2.5 × 10⁻⁶ m²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 m³</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1000 litres</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 L = 1000 cm³</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#7a4fd0\">●</span> 3. Magnetic — weber, tesla, A/m, henry</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#f1eafd;color:#7a4fd0\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#f1eafd;color:#7a4fd0\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#f1eafd;color:#7a4fd0\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">1 Wb (weber)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 V·s = 10⁸ maxwell</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">flux φ; 1 mWb = 10⁻³ Wb</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">1 T (tesla)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 Wb/m² = 10⁴ gauss</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">flux density B = φ / A</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">H (field strength)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">A/m (ampere-turns per metre)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 oersted = 1000/4π = 79.58 A/m</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">MMF</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">A or AT (ampere-turns)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">MMF = N I</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">1 H (henry)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 Wb/A = 1 V·s/A</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">inductance L = Nφ / I</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">μ₀</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">4π × 10⁻⁷ H/m</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">permeability of free space</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#d18a0e\">●</span> 4. Charge, capacitance &amp; current density — coulomb, farad, A/m²</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#fff5d4;color:#d18a0e\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#fff5d4;color:#d18a0e\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#fff5d4;color:#d18a0e\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 C (coulomb)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 A·s</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">Q = I t: 10 A for 4 min = 2400 C</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 Ah</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">3600 C</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 mAh = 3.6 C</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 electron</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1.602 × 10⁻¹⁹ C</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 C = 6.24 × 10¹⁸ electrons</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 F (farad)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 C/V</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">C = Q / V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 μF</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10⁻⁶ F = 1000 nF = 10⁶ pF</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 nF = 10⁻⁹ F · 1 pF = 10⁻¹² F</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">ε₀</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">8.854 × 10⁻¹² F/m</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">permittivity of free space</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 A/mm²</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10⁶ A/m²</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">current density J = I / A: 5 A in 2.5 mm² = 2 A/mm²</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",[]],"1446":["<h4 style=\"color:#1f4e79;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">Units &amp; conversions — continued</h4><p style=\"color:#555555\">Change any unit in one step: W ↔ kW, Wb, C, F, rad/s ↔ rpm, ° ↔ rad, K, N·m, A/m², dB, SI prefixes.</p><p style=\"font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#d63a4a\">●</span> 5. Angle &amp; speed — degree, radian, rad/s, rpm</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#fde9ec;color:#d63a4a\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#fde9ec;color:#d63a4a\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#fde9ec;color:#d63a4a\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">π rad</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">180°</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">2π rad = 360°</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">1 rad</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">57.3°</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1° = π/180 = 0.01745 rad</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">30° · 45° · 60° · 90°</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">π/6 · π/4 · π/3 · π/2</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">120° = 2π/3 · 270° = 3π/2</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">rpm → rad/s</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">ω = 2πN / 60 (× 0.1047)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1500 rpm = 157.1 rad/s · 3000 rpm = 314.2 rad/s</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">rad/s → rpm</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">N = 60 ω / 2π (× 9.549)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">100 rad/s = 955 rpm</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">1 rps</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">60 rpm</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">rps = revolutions per second</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">ω = 2πf</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">50 Hz → 314.16 rad/s</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">60 Hz → 377 rad/s</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">electrical angle</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">(P/2) × mechanical angle</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">4-pole: 1 mechanical rev = 720° electrical</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#14857a\">●</span> 6. Time &amp; frequency — second, hertz</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#e3f5f3;color:#14857a\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#e3f5f3;color:#14857a\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#e3f5f3;color:#14857a\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">1 h</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">60 min = 3600 s</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1 day = 86 400 s</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">1 ms · 1 μs · 1 ns</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">10⁻³ s · 10⁻⁶ s · 10⁻⁹ s</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">milli, micro, nano</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">T = 1/f</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">50 Hz → 20 ms</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1 kHz → 1 ms · 1 MHz → 1 μs</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">1 Hz</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">1 cycle per second</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">f = PN/120 for a machine</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#2f6fd0\">●</span> 7. Temperature — kelvin, °C, °F</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#e8f1fd;color:#2f6fd0\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#e8f1fd;color:#2f6fd0\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#e8f1fd;color:#2f6fd0\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">K</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">°C + 273.15 (≈ 273)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">27 °C = 300 K</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">°C</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">K − 273</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">0 K = −273 °C (absolute zero)</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">°F</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">(9/5) °C + 32</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">100 °C = 212 °F · 0 °C = 32 °F</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">°C</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">(°F − 32) × 5/9</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">−40 °C = −40 °F</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2f6fd0;font-weight:700\">a change of 1 K</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">a change of 1 °C</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">temperature rise is the same in K and °C</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#2e8b57\">●</span> 8. Force, torque &amp; pressure — newton, newton-metre</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#e8f6ea;color:#2e8b57\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#e8f6ea;color:#2e8b57\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#e8f6ea;color:#2e8b57\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 N (newton)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">1 kg·m/s²</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1 kN = 1000 N</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 kgf</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">9.81 N</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">weight = m g</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 N·m (torque)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">1 J when used as energy</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1 kgf·m = 9.81 N·m</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">T from P and N</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">T = 9.55 P / N (N·m, W, rpm)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1 kW at 1000 rpm → 9.55 N·m</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 Pa</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">1 N/m²</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1 bar = 10⁵ Pa</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#2e8b57;font-weight:700\">1 atm</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"font-weight:700\">1.013 × 10⁵ Pa = 760 mm Hg</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\" style=\"color:#3d4a60\">1 kg/cm² = 0.981 bar</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",[]],"1447":["<h4 style=\"color:#1f4e79;font-size:1.75em;font-weight:700\">Units &amp; conversions — continued</h4><p style=\"color:#555555\">Change any unit in one step: W ↔ kW, Wb, C, F, rad/s ↔ rpm, ° ↔ rad, K, N·m, A/m², dB, SI prefixes.</p><p style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#7a4fd0\">●</span> 9. Decibels — dB</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#f1eafd;color:#7a4fd0\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#f1eafd;color:#7a4fd0\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#f1eafd;color:#7a4fd0\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">power ratio</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">dB = 10 log₁₀ (P₂/P₁)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">×2 power = 3 dB · ×10 = 10 dB · ×100 = 20 dB</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">voltage / current ratio</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">dB = 20 log₁₀ (V₂/V₁)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">×2 voltage = 6 dB · ×10 = 20 dB</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">−3 dB</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">half power = 0.707 voltage</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">cut-off / bandwidth point</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">0 dB</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">ratio 1 (no gain, no loss)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">negative dB = loss</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">dBm</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10 log₁₀ (P / 1 mW)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">0 dBm = 1 mW · 30 dBm = 1 W</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#7a4fd0;font-weight:700\">1 neper</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">8.686 dB</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">Np = ln of the voltage ratio</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#d18a0e\">●</span> 10. Resistance, conductance &amp; light</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#fff5d4;color:#d18a0e\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#fff5d4;color:#d18a0e\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#fff5d4;color:#d18a0e\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 kΩ · 1 MΩ</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10³ Ω · 10⁶ Ω</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">4.7 kΩ = 4700 Ω</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 S (siemens)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 / Ω (mho)</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">conductance G = 1 / R</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">resistivity</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">Ω·m; 1 Ω·mm²/m = 10⁻⁶ Ω·m</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">copper ρ = 1.72 × 10⁻⁸ Ω·m</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d18a0e;font-weight:700\">1 lux</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 lumen/m²</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 foot-candle = 10.76 lux</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#d63a4a\">●</span> 11. SI prefixes — multiply by</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#fde9ec;color:#d63a4a\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#fde9ec;color:#d63a4a\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#fde9ec;color:#d63a4a\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">T (tera) · G (giga)</td><td style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10¹² · 10⁹</td><td>1 GW = 10⁹ W</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">M (mega) · k (kilo)</td><td style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10⁶ · 10³</td><td>1 MΩ = 10⁶ Ω</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">m (milli) · μ (micro)</td><td style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10⁻³ · 10⁻⁶</td><td>1 mA = 10⁻³ A</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#d63a4a;font-weight:700\">n (nano) · p (pico)</td><td style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10⁻⁹ · 10⁻¹²</td><td>1 pF = 10⁻¹² F</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-size:1.25em;font-weight:700\"><span style=\"color:#14857a\">●</span> 12. Other units used on the cards</p><div class=\"rtw\"><table class=\"rt rc\"><thead><tr><th style=\"background:#e3f5f3;color:#14857a\">Unit</th><th style=\"background:#e3f5f3;color:#14857a\">= equals</th><th style=\"background:#e3f5f3;color:#14857a\">Example / note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">A/s (ampere per second)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">rate of change of current, di/dt</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">V = L di/dt → 1 V = 1 H × 1 A/s</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">Wb/s (weber per second)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 V</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">Faraday: e = N dφ/dt</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">V/m (volt per metre)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 N/C</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">electric field E = V/d; 1 kV/cm = 10⁵ V/m</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">V·m (volt-metre)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">unit of electric flux</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">Gauss&#x27;s law: flux = Q/ε₀</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">C·m (coulomb-metre)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">electric dipole moment p = q d</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">1 debye ≈ 3.34 × 10⁻³⁰ C·m</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">J/m³ (joule per cubic metre)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1 N/m² = 1 Pa</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">energy density u = ½εE² or B²/2μ</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">per °C (1/°C)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">per kelvin (1/K) — same size</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">α of copper ≈ 0.00393 /°C at 20 °C</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">s⁻¹ and s⁻²</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">1/s = Hz (also rad/s); 1/s²</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">K<sub>v</sub> has unit s⁻¹, K<sub>a</sub> has s⁻²</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">kV, MVA</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">10³ V; 10⁶ VA</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">Z<sub>base</sub> = (kV)²/MVA ohm</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">kW/km</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">power loss per km of line</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">corona loss per km per phase</td></tr><tr><td style=\"color:#14857a;font-weight:700\">% (percent)</td><td data-h=\"= equals\" style=\"color:#1b2a4a;font-weight:700\">× 1/100</td><td data-h=\"Example / note\">efficiency 95 % = 0.95; pu × 100 = %</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",[]]}